From: Yunang Chen <yunang@google.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Keep unified APT lock imports out of MODULE.bazel.lock

A unified apt.import_lock declares every package, file-map, catalog and
hub repository from the reviewed source, request and lock files. Bazel
stored all of those repository specifications in the workspace
MODULE.bazel.lock because the extension returned no metadata, although
the import reads only tracked files and performs no index or network
access. Return reproducible metadata on this path so Bazel keeps the
repositories in its output-base cache instead. Generated repositories,
lock validation and the resolver/export path are unchanged.

Origin: SONiC lockfile size analysis of sonic-build-infra, where the
unified import accounted for almost all of the workspace lockfile.
Upstream status: SONiC-specific; upstream has no apt.import_lock.

Signed-off-by: Yunang Chen <yunang@google.com>
--- a/apt/extensions.bzl
+++ b/apt/extensions.bzl
@@ -267,7 +267,11 @@
     imports, _ = selected_lock_tags(mctx, require_one_root_lock = unified)
     if imports and not updates and unified:
         declare_locked_imports(mctx, [], installs, source_document)
-        return
+
+        # This path only reads tracked source, request and lock files. Bazel
+        # can recompute it exactly, so keep its repositories out of the
+        # workspace MODULE.bazel.lock.
+        return mctx.extension_metadata(reproducible = True)
     previous = {}
     for tag in updates:
         if tag.previous_lock:
